.B "tacctl __complete"
for the words. The bash script asks for the words alone (a second Tab lists
them in columns, as the shell does); the zsh and fish scripts ask for a
description of each sub-command, each flag (after the value it takes) and each
verb word after a name (the six words of
.BR "scope mgmt-acl lab" ),
each at most 72 characters and ending in \(lq...\(rq when cut. Live names
(users, groups, scopes, backends, listeners, backups; a device or host with
its vendor and scope) come from
.BR "sudo -n tacctl" ,
