.BR _ " and " \- ):
a name with upper case is refused with the lower\-case spelling to use, and a
user that exists with upper case keeps working as it is
.RB ( "tacctl config validate"
lists it). A period is refused: it cannot be part of a Linux account name, and
every user has an account on the tacctl server.
Prompts for the password with confirmation. If
.BI --hash " hash"
is given, the bcrypt hash is used directly and no password is prompted
(use this when users self-generate a hash; see
.BR "tacctl hash commands" ).
A lone
.B \-
as the hash reads it from one line of standard input (typed without echo at a
terminal), so it is not on the command line, where sudo's log records it and
.BR ps (1)
shows it while the command runs.
