the default is no, the answer is never taken from
.B \-\-yes
or any other option, and with no terminal the warning is all. Yes runs
.B "host sync"
of just those hosts, one after the other. The notices follow one rule: INFO
says what was done (the change, the restart, the sync); WARN says that
something failed or that the operator has to act (a sync that failed, hosts
left to sync, a device that still accepts a user who must change the
password); a fact is said once.
.PP
Reserved usernames
.RB ( root
and
.BR tacquito )
are rejected: both are local OS accounts that tacquito resolves outside
the YAML. Create an operator-specific account instead (for example,
.BR "tacctl user add jsmith superuser" ).
