Cisco devices enforce these rules live over TACACS+. Once any group has rules,
.B tacctl config cisco
emits
.B aaa authorization commands \fIlevel\fB default group TACACS-GROUP local
for every privilege level a group uses, and
.BR "aaa authorization config-commands" ,
and IOS asks tacquito for every command. A level where some group has no
rules gets the line commented out, naming the group and the fix
.RB ( "group commands default \fIgroup\fB permit" ):
without the fix the server denies that group every command.
Junos devices do not use these rules: the server sends them each group's own
deny sets
.RB ( "group junos" ).
