fix, and a staging /32 still pending for it),
.B Address
(the recorded address, the previous one and when it changed),
.B "Host keys"
(the pinned keys' SHA256 fingerprints and the command that shows them on the
host),
.B Sightings
(last and first seen, by which user over which backend, the NAS-Identifier),
.B Notices
(the open ones with their remedies and a count of the acknowledged ones),
.B Accounts
(the tacctl users the next sync makes there: name, tier, UID and groups;
disabled users counted, not listed),
.B "Last sync"
(when, by whom, the result or the reason it failed, the client script
protocol, and the accounts it created, updated and removed) and
.B "Host facts"
(the OS from /etc/os-release, sshd's version, the PAM module with its version,
and useradd's UID range from /etc/login.defs, as that sync read them). The
last two come from
.IR /etc/tacctl/hosts/ name .json ,
written by every
.B "host enroll"
and
.B "host sync"
(a failed sync too) and removed by
.BR "host unenroll" ;
a host with no such record shows
.BR "no record under this name" .
They are only shown, never used to decide anything. A host with a break\-glass
hold has a
.B Break\-glass
section first (the hold's time, age, user and reason, the address the server
does not answer and the release command;
.B breakglass
in
.BR \-\-json ).
.B \-\-check
logs in read-only, as
.B "host target"
