console unless disabled or of tier none, whatever their scopes, and it takes
no
.BR \-\-scope .
.B \-\-server
is the address devices and hosts reach this server at (an address behind NAT or
a VPN that is not on this machine is taken; a host name,
.BR 0.0.0.0 ,
.BR :: ,
a loopback, link\-local, multicast or broadcast address, or an IPv4\-mapped IPv6
address is not); without it the recorded address is
used, else the address of the interface with the default route, said in one
line; this machine's own PAM client always connects to
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
the address is what devices and other hosts use. It is recorded as
.B server.addresses
in
.I tacctl.yaml
(a list that holds one address for now), and
.B "host enroll \-\-local \-\-server"
.I address
changes it. An install from before whose server is registered in a scope that
serves the server alone is taken over by the next
.B "host sync"
of the server or
.BR "host enroll \-\-local" ,
its secret kept (a default\-scope marker on it is cleared); one that also serves hosts or devices is left to them, and
.B "host enroll \-\-local"
