interrupted puts the prefixes back and takes the new scope out again. A
.B "host sync"
of the server repairs its login when it was changed by hand
.RB ( "Repaired the managed server login." ).
.B "host move"
of this server is not a move: its login is set up by
.BR "host enroll \-\-local" .
.B "host forget"
and
.B "host unenroll"
of the server take the scope with the registration, its
.I tacctl.yaml
keys too, as
.B "scope remove"
does. The scope name
.B tacctl
is reserved: no command creates, edits, looks up or lists it (the JSON of
.B "host list"
and
.B "host show"
has no scope for the server), and the refusal of a prefix its login holds names
no command. A scope of that name from
an earlier release that answers an address other than this server's own login
addresses is the operator's: it is listed and edited like any other, and
.BR "host enroll \-\-local" ,
the sync of the server and
.B "config validate"
stop with one line until it is renamed
.RB ( "scope rename tacctl" " " "new\-name" ).
