.\" END GENERATED: command store show
.TP
.B "store import " "[ \-\-check | \-\-force ] [ \-\-replace ] [ " file " ]"
Import an old-style
.I tacquito.yaml
(default: the live one) into the store.
.B \-\-check
writes nothing and reports what would happen and whether the rendered config
is equivalent. Also the way to keep a hand edit of
.I tacquito.yaml
that
.B config validate
reports as drift. After an import every custom group at priv-lvl 15 without a
tier setting gets
.B superuser
recorded in
.I tacctl.yaml
(a line each; the same step as
.BR upgrade ),
and when this server is enrolled a red line says that users whose tier
fell keep their old groups until
.BR "host sync" .
A rendered file whose users section names users it cut out of their scopes (a
required password change, an emergency lockdown: a
.B "# tacctl-carved reason= protocol= users="
comment) does not hold the scopes they had, so each is listed as something the
store cannot represent and the import (and
.BR \-\-check )
fails unless
.B \-\-force
is given. A required password change, which no rendered file holds, is carried
over from the existing store
.RB ( \-\-replace ),
as the password dates are: an import never lifts it. The scope
.B tacctl
of a rendered file (the login of the server it came from, which every user is
in) is not imported and is taken out of the users' scopes, in one line; a
server registered in its own keeps it.
.\" BEGIN GENERATED: command store import
