.B add
reads the device's
.B sysObjectID.0
and
.B sysDescr.0
in one request and says which vendor they name
.RI ( "The device says it is Cisco IOS Software, vendor cisco (SNMP sysObjectID" " ...)" ).
An enterprise 9 sysObjectID with a sysDescr that starts
.B "Cisco IOS Software"
or
.B "Cisco IOS XE Software"
is
.BR cisco ;
an enterprise 2636 sysObjectID with a sysDescr that names Junos is
.BR juniper ;
an enterprise 2634 sysObjectID is
.B wti
(a WTI unit's sysDescr is generic Linux text, so the enterprise is the only
evidence).
