.B ios\-syntax
says; without it a Cisco device is walked through in its syntax (the setting,
else the last pull's, else the modern syntax with one line,
.BR "# syntax: modern (no pull yet; ...)" ,
after the data block). Only a cisco, juniper or wti device has a walkthrough: a
vendor
.B other
is refused with
.BI "tacctl device vendor " "name cisco|juniper|wti" ,
an enrolled Linux host with
